{"availability":"available","full":"seanoliver/audioflare","name":"audioflare","description":"An all-in-one AI audio playground using Cloudflare AI Workers to transcribe, analyze, summarize, and translate any audio file.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"TypeScript","stars":486,"forks":39,"created":"2023-10-13T23:27:04Z","updated":"2025-08-21T18:30:12Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://audioflare.seanoliver.dev/","topics":["ai","cloudflare","distilbert","llama2","m2m100","openai","whisper"],"demo":"https://audioflare.seanoliver.dev/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:08.314Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:08.314Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:08.314Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T21:33:08.314Z","stars":486,"forks":39}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Audioflare emerged from my side project endeavors at Smol AI, specifically aimed at exploring the capabilities of Cloudflare AI workers. The project demonstrates a practical use case by orchestrating a series of AI workers to process an audio file of up to 30 seconds. Here’s a walkthrough of the core functionality:","The current setup has its limitations; transcription is confined to 30 seconds, and the LLM model's performance on summarization could be better.","The underlying concept of Audioflare underscores the potential of Cloudflare AI workers by standardizing the AI API request framework, simplifying multi-step AI activities. Although the models in use have limitations and are marked as 'beta' by Cloudflare, there's a clear path toward enhancing this project as more models become available."],"features":["Initially, the audio file is transcribed using Cloudflare's Speech to Text worker, which is built on OpenAI's whisper API.","The transcribed text is then summarized using Cloudflare's LLM AI worker, based on Meta's llama-2-7b-chat-int8 model. It's worth noting that the LLM model struggles with lengthy prompts.","Sentiment analysis is performed on the transcribed text using Cloudflare's Text Classification AI worker, leveraging the Huggingface’s distilbert-sst-2-int8 model.","The transcribed text is translated into nine languages using Cloudflare's Translation AI workers, which utilize Meta's m2m100-1.2b model.","Performance Metrics:"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/seanoliver/audioflare/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"fd7b55633909d60069aa4f6da86c328664a4f88aba265e6803a6e02452b4bfa3","extractedAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:08.416Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:08.416Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Audioflare emerged from my side project endeavors at Smol AI, specifically aimed at exploring the capabilities of Cloudflare AI workers. The project demonstrates a practical use case by orchestrating a series of AI workers to process an audio file of up to 30 seconds. Here’s a walkthrough of the core functionality:","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/seanoliver/audioflare/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Create a Cloudflare account","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/seanoliver/audioflare/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Install Wrangler and login","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/seanoliver/audioflare/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"fd7b55633909d60069aa4f6da86c328664a4f88aba265e6803a6e02452b4bfa3","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/seanoliver/audioflare/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:08.417Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2025-08-21T18:30:12Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/seanoliver/audioflare/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:08.418Z","hash":"fd7b55633909d60069aa4f6da86c328664a4f88aba265e6803a6e02452b4bfa3","originalBytes":9809,"storedBytes":9809,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["cloudflare","text","workers","audio","project","top","using","back","transcribed